        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #0E1C42; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 10px;">A few words in this lesson are worth reviewing before you read. They are shown in bold with a dotted line. Hover over one to see what it means.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>amendment</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of amendment" onclick="speakGloss(event,'amendment')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(uh-MEND-ment)</span>: A change or addition to a constitution.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>bond</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of bond" onclick="speakGloss(event,'bond')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(BOND)</span>: A loan to a government. The government sells bonds to people, and promises to pay the money back with interest.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>checks and balances</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of checks and balances" onclick="speakGloss(event,'checks and balances')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(CHEKS and BAL-un-sez)</span>: A way of sharing power so that each part of government can limit the others.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>home rule</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of home rule" onclick="speakGloss(event,'home rule')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(HOHM ROOL)</span>: The right of a city to write its own charter, the plan for how the city is run.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>property tax</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of property tax" onclick="speakGloss(event,'property tax')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(PROP-er-tee TAX)</span>: A tax based on the value of land and buildings that a person owns.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>revenue</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of revenue" onclick="speakGloss(event,'revenue')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(REV-uh-noo)</span>: The money a government takes in.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>sales tax</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of sales tax" onclick="speakGloss(event,'sales tax')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(SAYLZ TAX)</span>: A tax added to the price of things people buy.</div>
